# bubble: a bubble sort that sorts its own picture
#
#     $ vonal run examples/bubble.vsr
#     0 1 2 3 4 5 6 7
#
# Row 7 holds the eight values, as the sizes of eight discs. The program sorts
# that row of the field in place, so the picture rearranges itself into a
# rising staircase as it runs. `vonal trace examples/bubble.vsr out.gif` shows
# it happening; examples/bubble.gif is that animation.
#
# One counter does the whole sort. k runs 0 to 48 and j = k mod 7, so the 49
# iterations are seven passes of seven adjacent comparisons, which is enough to
# sort eight elements. Nothing tracks whether a pass changed anything, so it
# always runs the full 49: a shorter program for a slower sort.
#
# Column 0 seeds k and drops the eye into row 2. The loop is entered at column
# 1, which leaves the turn-east at column 0 to double as the wrap point, and
# the stack is [k] at both ends of the row so running off the east edge wraps
# to the row's own start.
#
# Row 3 is the swap. The compare at column 14 turns south only when a > b, and
# the detour re-reads both values from the field rather than carrying them, so
# only j has to survive the branch. It runs west, wraps once, and climbs at
# column 15 onto a turn-east: that turn is not decoration. The detour arrives
# heading north, and without it the eye would sail up out of the loop.
#
# Leaving the loop is awkward for one reason: the detour fills row 3 edge to
# edge, so there is no way down through it. The eye climbs column 23 instead
# and wraps over the top of the torus into row 7, then into row 6. On the way
# it pops k and pushes m = 0 for the printing loop, using two cells that are
# free precisely because column 23 is the one column nothing else needs.
#
# Row 6 prints the sorted row and row 5 adds the newline. Rows 1, 4 and the
# unreached ends of the others are push discs whose sizes are a swell, as in
# vega: instructions that never execute, carrying the composition.
%plate 24x8

v1.5  o1.5  o1.5  o1.5  o1.5  o1.5  o1.5  o1.5  o1.5  o1.5  o1.5  o1.5  o1.5  o1.5  o1.5  o1.5  o1.5  o1.5  o1.5  o1.5  o1.5  o1.5  o1.5  o1.5
o1.5  o1.7  o1.6  o1.6  o1.6  o116  o116  o116  o126  o126  o126  o126  o126  o126  o126  o126  o116  o116  o116  o1.6  o1.6  o1.6  o1.7  %2.5
>1.5  %1.7  o176  #5.6  %1.5  %1.5  o177  @1.7  %3.7  o117  #1.7  o177  @1.7  D1.7  v2.7  >1.7  %2.7  o117  #1.5  %1.5  o166  o216  D3.7  ^2.5
%3.5  @2.7  o176  %5.6  o135  @1.5  o177  %1.7  #1.6  o116  %4.5  @1.5  o175  %1.5  <1.6  ^1.6  <1.7  <1.7  <1.5  @2.5  o176  %5.6  o137  %1.5
o1.5  o117  o116  o126  o125  o135  o147  o147  o156  o156  o165  o165  o165  o165  o156  o156  o147  o147  o135  o125  o126  o116  o117  o1.5
o1.5  o1.7  o1.6  o116  o125  o125  o137  o137  o137  >1.7  o117  o227  +2.7  ...7  o147  o137  o137  o137  o125  o125  o116  o1.6  o1.7  o1.5
<1.5  <1.7  <1.6  <1.6  <1.6  <1.6  <1.6  <1.6  <1.6  ^2.6  D3.6  o2.6  o116  %1.6  #1.6  o116  +2.6  o2.6  o146  +1.6  @1.6  o176  %1.7  <1.5
